Z||000000||TwisT||02-23-2001||08:43 PM||||FINALLY!!!  <P>I've been twiddling my thumbs at home with no Fiero to work on for about 6 months.  Today,  I finally got nerve enough to grab a shovel,  and with the help of a skid loader,  dug my '88 GT out of it's roof-high snow drift at my old work place.  It has been sitting there since last fall,  when I began the disassembly process for a new paint job (it's going to be Viper Red for those who are curious).<P>It fired right up and sat there growling as it always has.  After tons (felt like it anyway) of snow was moved and the car cover RIPPED off of it (it was a frozen and ripped mess),  I drove it just down the road to the shop where I work.  <P>I parked it in the shop,  where I proceeded to give it a THOROUGH steam-cleaning,  vac and general check-over.<P>Have you ever been away from your Fiero for a good amount of time?  ...And when you finally see it again and/or drive it,  you suddenly appreciate and admire the car more than before???<P>I DID...  today!<P>Anyways...  My Fiero enthusiasim just got a HUGE boost today,  seeing my baby once again in the flesh.  That's saying a lot since it hardly LOOKS like one right now.  Here's how she looks at the moment:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stripped1.JPG"> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stripped2.JPG"> <P><BR>...And here's why she's in need of a new coat of paint:<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fire1.JPG"> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fire2.JPG"> <P><BR>Not pretty,  huh?  The above pictures were taken after my mother's '85 GT (yes,  my mother even drives Fieros!) EXPLODED into flames late one night...  we don't know why.  My GT happened to be parked right beside it when it happened.  Needless to say,  plastic and fire don't mix!<P>Anyways...  they say,  "The past doesn't equal the future."  Here's what she's going to look like within a year:<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/italfiero.JPG"> <P><BR>Sorry about the intense bandwidth usage!!!<P>Brett  <P><BR>    ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-23-2001||09:31 PM||||Man I know what you mean.  Doing a big resto on my 87 coupe, and we are also going to paint it.  Mine's not as torn down on the outside as yours, but there are only two things left in the interior:  Steering column and headliner.  All else are wires and down to the bare frame.<P>Im going to be so happy when I can drive it again.  It's going to look so much better and have more toys in it.<P>The forum is the only way I keep my sanity!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
